1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,208
Your first hard paper can feel like a
wall of unfamiliar words. PaperPilot keeps

2
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:10,045
the paper in view and turns your questions
into a source-linked learning map.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,230
This is our rehearsed Attention
Is All You Need demo, not an

4
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:25,025
unseen-paper test. The real PDF scrolls
continuously. Its automatic map covers

5
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:29,819
document structure; it does not
mean an agent understood every page.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,825
I highlight the passage I want
explained, give it a question, and

7
00:00:37,825 --> 00:00:42,247
add that highlight to the graph.
The annotation starts with me,

8
00:00:42,247 --> 00:00:46,670
on the paper. Its text and location
become an immutable source.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,688
Now the browser agent uses six
bounded WebMCP tools to read my

10
00:00:58,688 --> 00:01:04,376
focus, inspect the graph, navigate sources,
stage explanations, and edit graph ideas

11
00:01:04,376 --> 00:01:09,590
and annotations. These receipts show
actual calls, not just registered tools.

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,558
The agent adds a linked concept and
question. Selecting the idea takes

13
00:01:20,558 --> 00:01:26,115
me back to the source. Its explanation
separates the paper’s evidence from

14
00:01:26,115 --> 00:01:31,209
teaching examples, interpretation, and
uncertainty. Save or discard remains my choice.

15
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,689
If an edit does not help,
I press Undo. Redo brings

16
00:01:41,689 --> 00:01:45,952
it back. The graph and annotations
change visibly, and their

17
00:01:45,952 --> 00:01:50,215
recorded digests return to the
expected state without erasing history.

18
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,302
For figures, I can describe
a page region and connect it

19
00:01:59,302 --> 00:02:03,213
to the map. This is locator-only
evidence: it identifies where

20
00:02:03,213 --> 00:02:07,125
to look, not proof that the
agent inspected the pixels.

21
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:16,263
PaperPilot is browser-local, keeps original
PDF bytes unchanged, and offers no PDF

22
00:02:16,263 --> 00:02:23,026
export. The evidence trail records what happened,
not scientific truth. Human accessibility

23
00:02:23,026 --> 00:02:29,790
review is still pending. Read, question,
connect, and return to the paper.
